hadiths[115]{hadithnumber,text}:
"109101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"109102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"109201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"109202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"109301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father said about the word of Allah"
"109302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father said about the word of Allah"
"109401","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"109402","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Abdullah ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"109501","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"109502","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"109601","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah were marrying off their daughters and they did not consult them. Malik said"
"109602","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah were marrying off their daughters and they did not consult them. Malik said"
"109701","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah and Sulayman ibn Yasar said about the virgin given by her father in marriage without her permission"
"109702","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah and Sulayman ibn Yasar said about the virgin given by her father in marriage without her permission"
"109801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah"
"109802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Malik from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah"
"109901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"109902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab had said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"110001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that the daughter of Ubaydullah ibn Umar whose mother was the daughter of Zayd ibn al- Khattab"
"110002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that the daughter of Ubaydullah ibn Umar whose mother was the daughter of Zayd ibn al- Khattab"
"110101","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz during his khalifate"
"110102","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz during his khalifate"
"110201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab decided about the woman who was married by a man and the marriage had been consummated"
"110202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab decided about the woman who was married by a man and the marriage had been consummated"
"110301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Zayd ibn Thabit said"
"110302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Zayd ibn Thabit said"
"110401","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"110402","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"110501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd ar- Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi from his father that when the Messenger of Allah"
"110502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd ar- Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi from his father that when the Messenger of Allah"
"110601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said"
"110602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said"
"110701","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked about a woman who made a stipulation on her husband not to take her away from her town. Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"110702","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked about a woman who made a stipulation on her husband not to take her away from her town. Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"110801","Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Miswar ibn Rifaa al- Quradhi from az-Zubayr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn az-Zubayr that Rifaa ibn Simwal divorced his wife"
"110802","Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Miswar ibn Rifaa al- Quradhi from az-Zubayr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn az-Zubayr that Rifaa ibn Simwal divorced his wife"
"110901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha"
"110902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha"
"111001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when asked whether it was permissible for a man to return to his wife if he had divorced her irrevocably and then another man had married her after him and died before consummating the marriage"
"111002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when asked whether it was permissible for a man to return to his wife if he had divorced her irrevocably and then another man had married her after him and died before consummating the marriage"
"111101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"111102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"111201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"111202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"1113","[1113] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: chaste women are First wives, and this is due to the fact that God Almighty forbids adultery."
"111401","Yahya related to me from Malik from more than one source that when Abdullah ibn Masud was in Kufa"
"111402","Yahya related to me from Malik from more than one source that when Abdullah ibn Masud was in Kufa"
"111501","Malik said that a man who had committed fornication with a woman and the hadd-punishment had been applied to him for it"
"111502","Malik said that a man who had committed fornication with a woman and the hadd-punishment had been applied to him for it"
"111601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Abd ar-Rahman and Mujamma the sons of Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari from Khansa bint Khidam al-Ansariya that her father gave her in marriage and she had been previously married. She disapproved of that"
"111602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Abd ar-Rahman and Mujamma the sons of Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari from Khansa bint Khidam al-Ansariya that her father gave her in marriage and she had been previously married. She disapproved of that"
"111701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki that a case was brought to Umar about a marriage which had only been witnessed by one man and one woman . He said"
"111702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki that a case was brought to Umar about a marriage which had only been witnessed by one man and one woman . He said"
"111801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab and from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Tulayha al-Asadiya was the wife of Rushayd ath-Thaqafi. He divorced her"
"111802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab and from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Tulayha al-Asadiya was the wife of Rushayd ath-Thaqafi. He divorced her"
"111901","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar were asked about a man who had a free woman as a wife and then wanted to marry a slave-girl. They disapproved that he should combine the two of them"
"111902","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar were asked about a man who had a free woman as a wife and then wanted to marry a slave-girl. They disapproved that he should combine the two of them"
"112001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"112002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"112101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Abd ar- Rahman that Zayd ibn Thabit said that if a man divorced his slave-girl three times and then bought her"
"112102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Abd ar- Rahman that Zayd ibn Thabit said that if a man divorced his slave-girl three times and then bought her"
"112201","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked whether"
"112202","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked whether"
"112301","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about a man who had a slave-girl as a wife"
"112302","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about a man who had a slave-girl as a wife"
"112401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from his father that Umar ibn al- Khattab was asked about a woman and her daughter who were in the possession of the right hand"
"112402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from his father that Umar ibn al- Khattab was asked about a woman and her daughter who were in the possession of the right hand"
"112501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb that a man asked Uthman ibn Affan whether one could have intercourse with two sisters who one owned. Uthman said"
"112502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb that a man asked Uthman ibn Affan whether one could have intercourse with two sisters who one owned. Uthman said"
"112601","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said the like of that. Malik said that if a man had sexual relations with a female slave that he owned"
"112602","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said the like of that. Malik said that if a man had sexual relations with a female slave that he owned"
"112701","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave his son a slave-girl and said"
"112702","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave his son a slave-girl and said"
"112801","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abd arRahman ibn al-Mujabbir said that Salim ibn Abdullah gave his son a slave-girl and said"
"112802","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abd arRahman ibn al-Mujabbir said that Salim ibn Abdullah gave his son a slave-girl and said"
"112901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Abu Nahshal ibn al-Aswad said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad"
"112902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Abu Nahshal ibn al-Aswad said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad"
"113001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan that he gave a slave-girl to a friend of his"
"113002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan that he gave a slave-girl to a friend of his"
"113101","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb that Umar ibn al-Khattab assigned a share for the grandfather (paternal) as people assign for him today."
"113102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Rafi' ibn Khadij: He married the daughter of Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari. She remained with him until she grew old. Then he married a young woman upon her, and he favored the young woman over her. She demanded divorce from him, so he divorced her once. Then he waited until she was nearly at the end of her waiting period (iddah), then he took her back. Then he again favored the young woman, so she demanded divorce, and he divorced her once, then took her back. Then he again favored the young woman, so she demanded divorce. He said: ""Whatever you wish. Only one divorce remains. If you wish, remain upon what you see of the favoritism, and if you wish, I will separate from you."" She said: ""Rather, I will remain upon the favoritism."" So he kept her upon that, and Rafi' saw no sin upon himself when she agreed to remain upon the favoritism."
"113201","Malik related to me that it reached him from Sulayman ibn Yasar that he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, Uthman ibn Affan, and Zayd ibn Thabit assigned for the grandfather with the brothers one-third. Malik said: The agreed-upon matter with us, and that which I found the people of knowledge in our land upon, is that the grandfather, the father of the father, does not inherit with the father anything at all. He is assigned a share with the male child and with the son's son, the male, one-sixth as an obligatory share (faridah). In other than that, as long as the deceased did not leave a brother or sister for his father, he is begun with one of them if he shares with him a named obligatory share, so they are given their obligatory shares. If there remains from the wealth one-sixth or more, the grandfather is assigned one-sixth as an obligatory share. Malik said: The grandfather and the brothers for the father and mother, if one of them shares with them a named obligatory share, one begins with whoever shares with them from the people of obligatory shares, so they are given their obligatory shares. Then whatever remains after that for the grandfather and the brothers of something, it is considered which of the two is better for the grandfather's portion: he is given one-third of what remains for him and for the brothers, or he is treated as one man among the brothers in what accrues to him and to them, so he shares with them with the like of the share of one of them, or one-sixth of the total capital. Whichever of these is best for the grandfather's portion is given to the grandfather, and whatever remains after that is for the brothers for the father and mother, for the male the like of the share of two females, except in one obligatory share where their division is otherwise. That obligatory share is: a woman dies and leaves her husband, her mother, her sister for her mother and father, her father, and her grandfather. For the husband is half, for the mother one-third, for the grandfather one-sixth, for the sister for the mother and father half. Then the grandfather's one-sixth and the sister's half are combined and divided into thirds: for the male the like of the share of two females. So for the grandfather is two-thirds of it, and for the sister one-third of it. Malik said: The inheritance of the brothers for the father with the grandfather, when there are no brothers for the father and mother with them, is like the inheritance of the brothers for the father and mother, the same: their male is like their male, and their female like their female. When the brothers for the father and mother and the brothers for the father gather, the brothers for the father and mother oppose the grandfather with their brothers for their father, so they prevent him from much of the inheritance by their number. They do not oppose him with the brothers for the mother, because if there were no one with the grandfather except them, they would not inherit anything with him, and the wealth would all be for the grandfather. So whatever the brothers get after the grandfather's portion is for the brothers from the father and mother, excluding the brothers for the father. The brothers for the father get nothing with them, except if the brothers for the father and mother are a single woman. If she is a single woman, she opposes the grandfather with her brothers for her father, whatever their number. So whatever accrues to them and to her is for her, excluding them, between her and completing her obligatory share. Her obligatory share is half of the total capital. If there is surplus in what is allotted to her and her brothers for her father beyond half of the total capital, it is for her brothers for her father, for the male the like of the share of two females. If nothing remains, they get nothing."
"113202","Yahya narrated to me from Malik, that it reached him that a man said to Abdillah ibn Abbas: \I have divorced my wife one hundred divorces.\"" He asked"
"113301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Uthman ibn
Ishaq ibn Kharasha that Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb said, ""A grandmother came
to Abu Bakr as-Siddiq and asked him for her inheritance. Abu Bakr said
to her, 'You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I do not know that
you have anything in the sunna of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah
bless him and grant him peace. Go away therefore, until I have
questioned the people.' (i.e.the Companions). He questioned the
people, and al-Mughira ibn Shuba said, 'I was present with the
Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he
gave the grandmother a sixth.' Abu Bakr said, 'Was there anybody else
with you?' Muhammad ibn Maslama al-Ansari stood up and said the like
of what al-Mughira said. Abu Bakr as-Siddiq gave it to her. Then the
other grandmother came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and asked him for her
inheritance. He said to her, ""You have nothing in the Book of Allah,
and what has been decided is only for other than you, and I am not one
to add to the fixed shares, other than that sixth. If there are two of
you together, it is between you. If eitherof you is left alone with
it, it is hers."""
"113302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abdullah and Hasan"
"113401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that Khawla ibn Hakim came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said"
"113402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that Khawla ibn Hakim came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said"
"113501","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Rabia ibn Abd ar- Rahman say that a slave could marry four women. Malik said"
"113502","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Rabia ibn Abd ar- Rahman say that a slave could marry four women. Malik said"
"113601","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he had heard that in the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"113602","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he had heard that in the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"113701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn
Muhammad ibn Amribn Hazm that Abdar-Rahman ibn Hanthala az-Zurqi was
informed by a mawla of Quraysh,who used to be known as Ibn Mursi, that
he was sitting with Umar ibn al-Khattab, and when they had prayed
dhuhr, he said, ""Yarfa! Bring that letter! (a letter which he had
written about the paternal aunt.) We asked about her and asked for
information about her."" Yarfa brought it to him. He called for a small
vessel or a drinking-bowl in which there was water. He erased the
letter in it. Then he said, ""Had Allah approved of you as an heir, we
would have confirmed you. Had Allah approved of you, we would have
confirmed you."""
"113702","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"113801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham who was the wife of Ikrima ibn Abi Jahl became muslim on the day of the conquest of Makka"
"113802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham who was the wife of Ikrima ibn Abi Jahl became muslim on the day of the conquest of Makka"
